description: PHP CMS implementation constraints.
globs: wordpress/**, wp-content/**, **/*.php
alwaysApply: false
---

# PHP CMS

- Preserve framework hooks, template override behavior, translations, nonces or CSRF tokens, escaping, capability checks, and plugin compatibility.
- Prefer framework APIs over direct SQL or ad hoc request handling.
- Sanitize input and escape output for the target context. Treat AJAX, REST, checkout, payment, upload, and account surfaces as security-sensitive.
- Verify with the narrowest relevant PHP, WP-CLI, browser, or runtime check available in the repo.
